{
	"_comment": "Cross-driver update-channel vectors, written by hand against channels.json. Every port replays this file: the JavaScript matcher (_shared/ui/update_channels.js, tools/test/test-update-channels-contract.cjs), the Lua port (_shared/lua/updater/channels.lua, one test per Lua driver) and the AHK port (windows/modules/updater/channels.ahk, tests/unit/test_updater_channel_registry.ahk). An empty string means no channel: the shared Lua JSON decoder turns a JSON null into a non-nil sentinel, so the shared data never uses null. tag: channel_for_tag(tag) must return channel. resolve: resolve(value) maps a persisted value or an alias to a channel id (exact and case-sensitive). visible: whether a release tag is listed in the Versions view of a channel (its own tags and those of every more stable channel). offer: should_offer(latest, current, selected, installed); a switch to another channel offers that channel's latest release even when semver orders it lower. pick: the tag pick_latest returns among tags, by semver order within the channel, first occurrence on a tie. newer_elsewhere: newer_elsewhere(releases, selected, installed) lists, in registry order, every channel other than the checked one whose latest release (pick rule) was published strictly after the installed build; the installed build's publish time is that of the first listed release of the same version, and a build that is not listed, or listed without a valid time, predates the whole list. A publish time is valid only as GitHub writes it (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ, UTC), so text order is time order; a channel whose latest release has no valid time is left out.",
